/* The course: units from A1 to C2, organised like a textbook (C2 units in course-c2.js).
   Each unit = objectives + teacher's note + vocabulary + grammar + reading/listening
   + speaking + writing + dictation + end-of-unit test. */

/* New speaking prompts used by the course (added to the existing ones). */
window.PROMPTS.push(
  { id: "b1-news", level: "B1", q: "Tell me about a piece of news that surprised you recently.", fr: "Parle-moi d'une nouvelle surprenante que tu as apprise récemment.", time: 90,
    phrases: ["I recently read that…", "According to…", "It was reported that…", "What surprised me was…", "I think it's because…"],
    model: "I recently read that a small town in Italy is selling houses for one euro. According to the article, the town is losing its population, so it's trying to attract new people. What surprised me was that you have to renovate the house within three years, which can be very expensive. Still, I think it's a clever idea, and if I had the money, I'd be tempted!" },
  { id: "b1-home", level: "B1", q: "Describe your ideal home.", fr: "Décris ta maison idéale.", time: 90,
    phrases: ["My ideal home would be…", "It would have…", "a place where…", "The thing that matters most to me is…", "It doesn't need to be…"],
    model: "My ideal home would be a bright flat in an old building, in a lively neighbourhood where I could walk everywhere. It would have big windows, high ceilings and a small balcony where I could have breakfast in summer. The thing that matters most to me is light, because I spend a lot of time at home. It doesn't need to be huge, but I'd love a separate room for my books and plants." },
  { id: "b1-habits", level: "B1", q: "How have your habits changed in the last few years?", fr: "Comment tes habitudes ont-elles changé ces dernières années ?", time: 90,
    phrases: ["I used to…, but now…", "I've started…", "I'm not used to… yet", "Most of my friends…", "It must be because…"],
    model: "My habits have changed quite a lot. I used to go to bed very late, but now I try to sleep before midnight. I've also started cooking more, because I used to eat a lot of ready meals. I'm not used to getting up early yet, but I'm getting better at it. Most of my friends have changed too: we spend less time in bars and more time walking. It must be because we're getting older!" },
  { id: "b1-job", level: "B1", q: "Describe your job, or a job you'd love to do.", fr: "Décris ton métier, ou un métier que tu aimerais faire.", time: 90,
    phrases: ["I work as…", "My job involves…", "What I enjoy most is…", "The hardest part is…", "I'm responsible for…"],
    model: "I work as a nurse in a children's hospital. My job involves looking after young patients and talking to their parents. What I enjoy most is the moment a child goes home in good health. The hardest part is working at night, because I never sleep well the next day. I'm responsible for a team of three nurses, which is tiring but very rewarding." },
  { id: "b2-future", level: "B2", q: "Where do you see yourself in five years?", fr: "Où te vois-tu dans cinq ans ?", time: 120,
    phrases: ["By then, I hope I'll have…", "I'll probably be…", "I was going to…, but…", "Ideally,…", "Whatever happens,…"],
    model: "That's a difficult question, but I'll try. By then, I hope I'll have reached a really good level of English, maybe even C1, which would allow me to travel and work abroad more easily. I'll probably still be doing the same job, but ideally with more time for my own projects. A few years ago, I was going to move to another city, but I'm glad I didn't. Whatever happens, I'd like to keep learning and to make sure I have enough time for the people I love." },
  { id: "b2-project", level: "B2", q: "Describe a project you're proud of.", fr: "Décris un projet que tu as mené et dont tu parles avec fierté.", time: 120,
    phrases: ["The project I'm proudest of is…", "The challenge was to…", "What made it work was…", "Looking back, I should have…", "It taught me that…"],
    model: "The project I'm proudest of is a shared garden that I started with my neighbours. The challenge was to turn an empty, rather depressing courtyard into a place people actually wanted to use. I spent a whole weekend just asking people what they would like, which turned out to be the best idea I had. What made it work was letting everyone choose one plant and look after it. Looking back, I should have asked the landlord for permission earlier, but it taught me that listening is the most important part of any project." },
  { id: "b2-fourday", level: "B2", q: "Should everyone work four days a week?", fr: "Tout le monde devrait-il travailler quatre jours par semaine ?", time: 120,
    phrases: ["On the one hand,…", "Supporters argue that…", "However,…", "Although…", "On balance,…"],
    model: "It's an attractive idea, but I'm not sure it would work for everyone. On the one hand, supporters argue that people would be more rested and more productive, and some trials seem to confirm that. On the other hand, it would be much harder to organise in hospitals, schools or shops, where someone has to be there every day. Although I'd personally love a three-day weekend, I think the answer depends on the sector. On balance, I'd say companies should be free to try it, rather than being forced to." },
  { id: "c1-place", level: "C1", q: "Describe a place that means a lot to you, and explain why.", fr: "Décris un lieu qui compte beaucoup pour toi, et explique pourquoi.", time: 150,
    phrases: ["What makes it special is…", "Having spent…", "It's not so much… as…", "Little did I know…", "Whenever I go back,…"],
    model: "There's a small beach in Brittany where my grandparents used to take us every summer. What makes it special is not so much the place itself, which is actually rather ordinary, as the memories attached to it. Having spent every August there until I was fifteen, I know every rock and every path. Little did I know, as a bored teenager, how much I would miss those long, slow afternoons. Whenever I go back now, I feel both nostalgic and strangely calm, as if time had slowed down." }
);

